---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Paros | Suites With Keith"
  description="Keith's Paros guide: where to stay, the room to book at each hotel, three perfect days, and the ferry rules that save your trip."
  current="guides"
  preload="/images/islands/paros-hero.jpg"
>

<header class="hero" style="min-height:min(80svh,760px);">
  <img class="hero-img" src="/images/islands/paros-hero.jpg" alt="Whitewashed lanes and bougainvillea on Paros" width="1201" height="1800" fetchpriority="high" />
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Destination guide &middot; The Cyclades</p>
    <h1 class="display-xl">Paros</h1>
    <p class="sub" style="font-family:var(--display); font-style:italic; font-size:1.2rem;">The island everyone quietly falls in love with.</p>
    <p class="stamp">The Greece Collection &middot; Issue No. 01 &middot; guide 04</p>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- verdict + glance -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="verdict reveal">
      <p>Paros is the island I recommend more every year. Beautiful beaches, exceptional restaurants, stylish hotels and authentic villages &mdash; without feeling overly polished. If you&rsquo;re looking for the Cyclades beyond the postcard version of Greece, start here.</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="kv reveal" style="margin-top:48px;">
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Best for</dt><dd>Couples, repeat Greece visitors, food lovers</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Ideal stay</dt><dd><b>3&ndash;5 nights</b> &mdash; two islands per week; three is a travel day disguised as a vacation</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Best months</dt><dd>May&ndash;June, September</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Don&rsquo;t miss</dt><dd>Naousa harbor after sunset &middot; lunch at a Crios beach club &middot; Kolymbithres&rsquo; granite coves &middot; a sunset stroll through Lefkes</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Getting around</dt><dd>Rent a car &mdash; the island is compact enough that everything feels within reach. Between islands, I arrange private boats and helicopters through Hoper.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- where to stay -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Where to stay</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">Four hotels, four different trips</h2>
      <p class="deck" style="margin-top:16px; max-width:44ch;">Each of these solves a different problem. The room line is the answer I&rsquo;m most often asked for &mdash; so it&rsquo;s first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards reveal">
      <a class="card" href="/hotels/cosme-paros.html">
        <img src="/images/hotels/cosme-1.jpg" alt="Cosme, Paros" width="1800" height="1013" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad">
          <span class="kicker">Stayed &middot; beachfront, walk to Naousa</span>
          <h3>Cosme</h3>
          <p><b>Book:</b> a base room, honestly &mdash; bigger than most junior suites. The beach out front, Naousa on foot, no car all week. From $950/night.</p>
          <span class="go">The full record &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/compare/cosme-vs-parilio.html">
        <img src="/images/hotels/parilio-1.jpg" alt="Parīlio, Paros" width="1800" height="1013" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad">
          <span class="kicker">Toured &middot; the design icon</span>
          <h3>Par&imacr;lio</h3>
          <p><b>Book:</b> a Sun Suite with private pool &mdash; the outdoor space is the point. Calm, architectural, minutes from Naousa. From $900/night.</p>
          <span class="go">Cosme or Par&imacr;lio? &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="#inquire">
        <img src="/images/hotels/vione-1.jpg" alt="Vione, Paros" width="1800" height="1013" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad">
          <span class="kicker">Toured &middot; adults-focused</span>
          <h3>Vione</h3>
          <p><b>Book:</b> a Junior Suite &mdash; surprisingly spacious, one of the island&rsquo;s best values. The spa was the most expansive I saw in the Cyclades. From $800/night.</p>
          <span class="go">Ask me about Vione &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="#inquire">
        <img src="/images/hotels/andronis-minois-1.jpg" alt="Andronis Minois, Paros" width="1800" height="1013" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad">
          <span class="kicker">Toured &middot; the resort stay</span>
          <h3>Andronis Minois</h3>
          <p><b>Book:</b> the Minois Blu Suite, sea view. Space, comfort and a proper resort pace &mdash; stay four nights minimum. From $700/night.</p>
          <span class="go">Ask me about Minois &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- three days -->
<section class="section band on-shadow">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Three perfect days</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">How I&rsquo;d spend them</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ledger reveal">
      <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">01</span><span class="d"><b>Arrive.</b> An afternoon at your hotel, then Naousa as the sun drops &mdash; the boutiques, the harbor, and a long dinner at Siparos while the waterfront comes alive.</span></div>
      <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">02</span><span class="d"><b>Discover.</b> Lefkes in the morning, lunch at To Balconi tou Aki in Aliki, an afternoon swim at Lageri, and dinner back in Lefkes at Santa Pacou. Don&rsquo;t miss sunset on the marble streets.</span></div>
      <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">03</span><span class="d"><b>Unwind.</b> A slow morning, the day at Crios Beach Club, and a last dinner at Parostia at Cosme &mdash; one of my favorite restaurants on the island.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="body-2 reveal" style="margin-top:26px; max-width:56ch;">Paros&rsquo; greatest strength is its scale: compact enough that a lazy beach day never feels like missing out. Slow down and let it unfold.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ferry rules -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Getting there</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">The ferry rules that save trips</h2>
    </div>
    <dl class="kv reveal">
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Rule 1</dt><dd>Never book the last ferry of the day. If it&rsquo;s cancelled, you&rsquo;ve lost a night.</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Rule 2</dt><dd>Fast ferries cancel in wind; slow ones usually don&rsquo;t. In shoulder season, take the slow boat.</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Rule 3</dt><dd>Don&rsquo;t fly home the same day you sail. Give yourself a night in Athens.</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Skip it all</dt><dd>A private boat between islands, or a helicopter direct &mdash; the thing I&rsquo;m asked to arrange most. It turns a lost travel day into a morning.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ask -->
<section class="section inquire" id="inquire">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="display-l reveal">Planning Paros?</h2>
    <p class="deck reveal" style="margin:18px auto 0; max-width:42ch;">Send me your dates. I&rsquo;ll tell you which hotel fits, which room to book, and how to get between islands without losing a day.</p>
    <form class="inquire-form reveal" action="https://formspree.io/f/mjgnadov" method="POST">
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Paros Inquiry" />
      <input type="hidden" name="hotel" value="Paros (guide)" />
      <input type="hidden" name="page" value="phase1/guides/paros" />
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      <div class="step1">
        <label for="q-when">When are you thinking?</label>
        <input id="q-when" type="text" name="travel_dates" placeholder="Mid September, 4 nights" required autocomplete="off" />
      </div>
      <div class="step2">
        <label for="q-name">And where do I send the recommendation?</label>
        <input id="q-name" type="text" name="name" placeholder="Name" required autocomplete="name" />
        <input id="q-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="Email" required autocomplete="email" />
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Send</button>
      <p class="note">Traveling within the next 30 days? You&rsquo;ll hear from me today.</p>
      <p class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
